exports[`HTML structure snapshot > matches the stored structure of a report that uses every part of the layout 1`] = `
"<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to the report</a>
<header class="top"><div class="wrap">
<p class="brand">ShipCheck</p>
<h1>Pre-launch report</h1>
<dl class="meta">
<div><dt>App</dt><dd><a href="https://myapp.example.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://myapp.example.com/</a></dd></div>
<div><dt>Date</dt><dd>13 November 2026, 17:57 UTC</dd></div>
<div><dt>Duration</dt><dd>2 seconds</dd></div>
<div><dt>AI model</dt><dd>None — automatic checks only</dd></div>
<div><dt>ShipCheck version</dt><dd>0.1.0</dd></div>
</dl>
</div></header>
<main id="main" class="wrap">
<section class="verdict v-checks-found-issues t-blocker" aria-labelledby="verdict-title">
<h2 id="verdict-title">Verdict</h2>
<p class="big">Automatic checks found issues</p>
<p>At least one is a blocker: fix it before you launch. ShipCheck did not use your app like a visitor, so a full check may find more.</p>
<ul class="counts" aria-label="Issues by severity"><li><span class="badge sev-blocker" title="Blocker: a new user cannot get through, or a secret is exposed">1 Blocker</span></li><li><span class="badge sev-major" title="Major: it works, but is broken or confusing for many users">1 Major</span></li><li><span class="badge sev-minor" title="Minor: polish and edge cases">1 Minor</span></li><li><span class="badge sev-info" title="Info: good to know, not a bug">1 Info</span></li></ul>
<p class="legend">Blocker = stops people using your app · Major = breaks or confuses many people · Minor = polish</p>
</section>
<section class="coverage" aria-labelledby="coverage-title">
<h2 id="coverage-title">What this report covers</h2>
<p class="check-type">Automatic checks only (no AI)</p>
<p>ShipCheck loaded your pages and checked them from the outside: hidden errors, broken links, phone screen layout, SEO and basic security. It did not sign up, log in or use any feature.</p>
<table class="cov">
<caption class="sr-only">What happened in each area</caption>
<thead class="sr-only"><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead>
<tbody><tr class="group"><th colspan="2" scope="colgroup">Using your app like a visitor (full check only)</th></tr><tr class="st-not-tested"><th scope="row">Sign-up</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">○</span> <span class="state">Not tested: this needs the full check</span></td></tr><tr class="st-problems s-major"><th scope="row">Log-in</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">⚠</span> <span class="state"><a href="#issue-2">1 problem</a></span><span class="why">Only partly tested: this needs the full check</span></td></tr><tr class="st-not-tested"><th scope="row">Main feature</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">○</span> <span class="state">Not tested: this needs the full check</span></td></tr><tr class="st-not-tested"><th scope="row">Forms (including wrong or missing input)</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">○</span> <span class="state">Not tested: this needs the full check</span></td></tr><tr class="st-not-tested"><th scope="row">Using it on a phone</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">○</span> <span class="state">Not tested: this needs the full check</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody><tr class="group"><th colspan="2" scope="colgroup">Automatic checks (always run)</th></tr><tr class="st-no-problems"><th scope="row">Phone screen layout</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> <span class="state">No problems found</span></td></tr><tr class="st-no-problems"><th scope="row">Hidden errors</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> <span class="state">No problems found</span></td></tr><tr class="st-no-problems"><th scope="row">Broken links</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> <span class="state">No problems found</span></td></tr><tr class="st-problems s-minor"><th scope="row">SEO</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">⚠</span> <span class="state"><a href="#issue-3">1 problem</a></span></td></tr><tr class="st-problems s-blocker"><th scope="row">Basic security</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">⚠</span> <span class="state"><a href="#issue-1">1 problem</a></span></td></tr><tr class="st-no-problems"><th scope="row">Accessibility</th><td><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> <span class="state">No problems found</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p class="why-differ">Automatic checks can’t find problems that only appear when someone uses the app, such as a sign-up that fails or a button that does nothing. That’s why a full check often finds more than automatic checks.</p>
<p><strong>Next step:</strong> Run the full check to test your app like a real visitor. You need a free AI key.</p>
<pre class="cmd"><code>npx @anjalipanwar/shipcheck https://myapp.example.com/</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://github.com/Anjalipanwar/shipcheck#get-a-free-ai-key" rel="noopener noreferrer">How to get a free AI key</a></p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="first-title">
<h2 id="first-title">Fix these first</h2>
<div class="panel"><ol class="first"><li><span class="badge sev-blocker">Blocker</span><a href="#issue-1">A secret key is visible to anyone who visits your app</a></li><li><span class="badge sev-major">Major</span><a href="#issue-2">Login shows no message when the password is wrong</a></li><li><span class="badge sev-minor">Minor</span><a href="#issue-3">Your home page has no description for search results</a></li></ol></div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="look-title">
<h2 id="look-title">Your app as ShipCheck saw it</h2>
<div class="panel"><div class="shots"><figure><button type="button" class="shot" data-shot="shot-2" aria-label="Enlarge screenshot: home page (desktop)"><img id="shot-2" src="data:image/jpeg;base64,…" alt="Screenshot: home page (desktop)"></button><figcaption>home page (desktop)<span class="zoom"> — click to enlarge</span></figcaption></figure></div></div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="issues-title">
<h2 id="issues-title">All issues (4)</h2>
<p class="legend">“Verified” means an automatic check measured it. “AI judgement” means the AI tester saw it while using the app — worth a quick look yourself.</p>
<h3>Login</h3>
<article class="card c-major" id="issue-2" aria-labelledby="issue-2-title">
<h4 id="issue-2-title">Login shows no message when the password is wrong</h4>
<ul class="badges">
<li><span class="badge sev-major">Major</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Functionality</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Desktop</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">AI judgement</span></li>
</ul>
<h5>What happened</h5><p>It broke.</p>
<h5>Why it matters</h5><p>People notice.</p>
<h5>Steps to reproduce</h5>
<ol class="steps"><li>Open the page.</li><li>Click the button.</li></ol>
<h5>Evidence</h5>
<div class="shots"><figure><button type="button" class="shot" data-shot="shot-1" aria-label="Enlarge screenshot: login failed (desktop)"><img id="shot-1" src="data:image/jpeg;base64,…" alt="Screenshot: login failed (desktop)"></button><figcaption>login failed (desktop)<span class="zoom"> — click to enlarge</span></figcaption></figure></div>
<p class="where">Where: <a href="https://myapp.example.com/login" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://myapp.example.com/login</a></p>
</article>
<h3>Security</h3>
<article class="card c-blocker" id="issue-1" aria-labelledby="issue-1-title">
<h4 id="issue-1-title">A secret key is visible to anyone who visits your app</h4>
<ul class="badges">
<li><span class="badge sev-blocker">Blocker</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Security</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Desktop and phone</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Verified</span></li>
</ul>
<h5>What happened</h5><p>It broke.</p>
<h5>Why it matters</h5><p>People notice.</p>
<h5>Steps to reproduce</h5>
<ol class="steps"><li>Open the page.</li><li>Click the button.</li></ol>
<h5>Evidence</h5>
<p class="where">Where: <a href="https://myapp.example.com/assets/app.js" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://myapp.example.com/assets/app.js</a></p>
<details><summary>Technical details (1 line)</summary><pre>Stripe secret key: sk_liv…eal1</pre></details>
<div class="fix">
<div class="fix-head"><h5>Fix prompt</h5><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="issue-1-prompt" aria-label="Copy fix prompt: A secret key is visible to anyone who visits your app">Copy</button></div>
<p class="hint">Paste this into Lovable, Bolt, Cursor or Claude Code.</p>
<pre id="issue-1-prompt">Remove the key from client-side code.</pre>
</div>
</article>
<article class="card c-info" id="issue-4" aria-labelledby="issue-4-title">
<h4 id="issue-4-title">Local address — HTTPS not checked</h4>
<ul class="badges">
<li><span class="badge sev-info">Info</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Security</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Desktop</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Verified</span></li>
</ul>
<h5>What happened</h5><p>It broke.</p>
<h5>Why it matters</h5><p>People notice.</p>
<h5>Evidence</h5>
<details><summary>Technical details (1 line)</summary><pre>a log line</pre></details>
</article>
<h3>Search and sharing (SEO)</h3>
<article class="card c-minor" id="issue-3" aria-labelledby="issue-3-title">
<h4 id="issue-3-title">Your home page has no description for search results</h4>
<ul class="badges">
<li><span class="badge sev-minor">Minor</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">SEO</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Desktop and phone</span></li>
<li><span class="tag">Verified</span></li>
</ul>
<h5>What happened</h5><p>It broke.</p>
<h5>Why it matters</h5><p>People notice.</p>
<h5>Steps to reproduce</h5>
<ol class="steps"><li>Open the page.</li><li>Click the button.</li></ol>
<h5>Evidence</h5>
<details><summary>Technical details (1 line)</summary><pre>No &lt;meta name=&quot;description&quot;&gt; found</pre></details>
<div class="fix">
<div class="fix-head"><h5>Fix prompt</h5><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="issue-3-prompt" aria-label="Copy fix prompt: Your home page has no description for search results">Copy</button></div>
<p class="hint">Paste this into Lovable, Bolt, Cursor or Claude Code.</p>
<pre id="issue-3-prompt">Add a &lt;meta name=&quot;description&quot;&gt; tag.</pre>
</div>
</article>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="worked-title">
<h2 id="worked-title">What worked</h2>
<div class="panel"><ul class="list worked"><li>Home page opens</li><li>Home page has a title</li></ul></div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="skipped-title">
<h2 id="skipped-title">What we couldn’t test</h2>
<div class="panel"><ul class="list skipped"><li>Signing up — needs an AI key</li></ul></div>
</section>
</main>
<footer><div class="wrap">
<p>ShipCheck is an automated pre-launch check. It is not a security audit and not a guarantee that the app is free of bugs.</p>
<p>Not checked: active security testing, completing a payment, emails the app sends, business rules beyond what is visible on screen, behaviour under heavy traffic, and native mobile apps.</p>
<p>Made with <a href="https://github.com/Anjalipanwar/shipcheck" rel="noopener noreferrer">ShipCheck</a> 0.1.0 — free and open source.</p>
</div></footer>
<dialog id="lightbox" aria-labelledby="lightbox-title">
<div class="bar"><strong id="lightbox-title" class="caption">Screenshot</strong><button type="button" data-close>Close</button></div>
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,…" alt="">
</dialog>
<div id="status" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>"
